Public Stata code accompanying the manuscript:

Persistence in reapplying to university after rejection: Associations with register-based mental health indicators and genetic endowment for educational attainment
Henrik Dobewall, Hannu Lehti, Outi Sirniö, and Maria Vaalavuo

The individual-level Finnish register and genetic data are restricted and cannot be shared by the authors.

## Analyses in the paper

The paper contains two separate analyses:

- **Application outcomes:** person-level analyses in the full analytic sample, distinguishing individuals who never applied, were rejected, or were directly accepted to university. These analyses are cross-sectional and do not use the discrete-time person-year structure.
- **Stop applying after experiencing rejection:** a longitudinal analysis restricted to university applicants whose first application ended in rejection. This analysis uses annual person-years and a logistic discrete-time hazard model.

The public code focuses on the data coding required for the second analysis. `DATA_DESCRIPTION.md` describes the data and variables used in both parts of the paper.

## Discrete-time coding

For the re-application analysis, follow-up starts in the year after the first rejected university application. Each subsequent year contributes one person-year while the individual remains at risk. `stop_apply = 1` in the first year in which no new university application is made; a gap year therefore counts as stop applying. Follow-up ends at stop applying, university admission, the four-year follow-up limit, or the end of observation. Years after age 24 are excluded.

`hakukerta` indexes annual time from the first application and is included as a categorical time variable in the logistic regression. The person-year risk-set construction, outcome coding, and time indicators make the logistic regression a discrete-time hazard model.

## Files

- `DATA_DESCRIPTION.md` — data sources, analytic samples, variable definitions, and timing.
- `01_build_discrete_time_sample.do` — constructs the post-rejection person-year risk set.
- `02_discrete_time_models.do` — estimates the discrete-time models and interaction analyses.

AI assisted the production of this repository. Full code available upon request.
